+    "# The artifact tokens\n",
+    "\n",
+    "A demo on the high-norm tokens of large ViTs (Darcet et al., *Vision Transformers Need Registers*): tokens\n",
+    "in uninformative patches that the model recycles to store global information. In NAVE they tend to form a\n",
+    "concept of their own, made of the most uncertain tokens.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "One reading: if the semantic concepts are compact and well separated, a token that averages them all\n",
+    "points far from each of them, and the average forms a separable concept of its own. This notebook measures,\n",
+    "block by block:\n",
+    "- the **norm** of the artifact tokens against the others;\n",
+    "- the **cosine** between the artifact concept's prototype and the **mean** of the other prototypes (close to 1\n",
+    "  if the artifacts are their average);\n",
+    "- the **separation** of the other concepts (mean cosine between their prototypes: lower is more separated);\n",
+    "- at the last block, **uncertainty against norm**, token by token.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Large, long-trained ViTs show artifacts most clearly: try `(\"vits16\", \"dino\")` and `(\"vits16\", \"imagenet\")`.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "**Needs:** `pip install \"nave-xai[animation]\"`. **Downloads:** none with ViT-Ti/16; about 90 MB per ViT-S/16."
